{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"d0998eba-85d9-4eb4-8f78-d029626a9e33","step_index":85,"state":"DONE","step_type":"agent_response","text_delta":"-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tests/test_conformance.py#L174) immediately fail with `AssertionError: True is not false : Tool 'get_note' ... returned isError: [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Object of type Decimal is not JSON serializable'}]`.\n- **Test Suite Execution:** With the fix applied, all 9 tests pass cleanly:\n  ```bash\n  $ python3 -m unittest discover -v -s tests\n  # Ran 9 tests in 0.001s: OK\n  $ PRODUCTION_DB=1 python3 -m unittest discover -v -s tests\n  # Ran 9 tests in 0.001s: OK\n  ```\n","duration_seconds":10.093551,"usage":{"input_tokens":4269,"output_tokens":3001,"thinking_tokens":167,"cache_read_tokens":110102,"total_tokens":7270}}}
{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"d0998eba-85d9-4eb4-8f78-d029626a9e33","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Following the guide *\"My tests passed because they agreed with me\"*, the following issues were identified and resolved, and client-style conformance tests were added:\n\n### Issues Found \u0026 Fixed\n\n1. **Test fake was too forgiving ([`db.py`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/db.py#L56-L68)):**\n   - [`FakeStore`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/db.py#L56) returned plain Python integers and floats, masking DynamoDB type semantics where numbers are deserialized as `Decimal` instances at all depths.\n   - **Fix:** Updated [`FakeStore.get`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/db.py#L62) and [`FakeStore.scan`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/db.py#L66) to pass items through [`_to_dynamo`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/db.py#L29), matching production [`DynamoStore`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/db.py#L42).\n\n2. **Uncoerced nested `Decimal` values breaking serialization ([`tools.py`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tools.py#L5-L13)):**\n   - [`tools._coerce`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tools.py#L5) only converted top-level `word_count` to `int`, leaving nested numbers in `stats` (`views`, `rating`, `revisions`) as `Decimal`.\n   - In production or with a realistic fake, calling [`get_note`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tools.py#L18) caused `json.dumps` to fail with `TypeError: Object of type Decimal is not JSON serializable`, resulting in [`server.py`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/server.py#L95) returning `isError: true` on every invocation.\n   - **Fix:** Updated [`_coerce`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tools.py#L5) to recursively coerce all `Decimal` values at any depth to JSON-friendly primitives (`int` if whole, `float` otherwise).\n\n3. **Tool parameter handling ([`server.py`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/server.py#L82)):**\n   - Guarded [`_call_tool`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/server.py#L81) with `arguments = arguments or {}` to gracefully handle `null` arguments.\n\n---\n\n### Tests Added ([`tests/test_conformance.py`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tests/test_conformance.py))\n\nAdded four new tests via [`ConformanceTest`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tests/test_conformance.py#L107) that interact exclusively through the real entry point [`server.handle()`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/server.py#L99):\n\n1. **[`test_initialize`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tests/test_conformance.py#L114):** Sends `initialize` through `server.handle()`, asserting valid JSON-RPC 2.0 structure, `protocolVersion`, `capabilities.tools`, and `serverInfo`.\n2. **[`test_tools_list_without_credentials`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tests/test_conformance.py#L133):** Requests `tools/list` without credentials to verify public discoverability and schema exposure.\n3. **[`test_call_tools_serializes_response`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tests/test_conformance.py#L149):** Calls each tool through `server.handle()`, asserting that calls do not return `isError: true` and that the entire response survives JSON serialization.\n4. **[`test_validate_against_published_output_schema`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tests/test_conformance.py#L174):** Dynamically extracts schemas from the `tools/list` response, verifies that `structuredContent` is present when `outputSchema` is declared, and validates all properties and nested objects recursively against the published schema using [`validate_schema`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tests/test_conformance.py#L15).\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n\n- **Mutation Check:** When reverting the [`_coerce`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tools.py#L5) fix, [`test_call_tools_serializes_response`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tests/test_conformance.py#L149) and [`test_validate_against_published_output_schema`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-with/repo/tests/test_conformance.py#L174) immediately fail with `AssertionError: True is not false : Tool 'get_note' ... returned isError: [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Object of type Decimal is not JSON serializable'}]`.\n- **Test Suite Execution:** With the fix applied, all 9 tests pass cleanly:\n  ```bash\n  $ python3 -m unittest discover -v -s tests\n  # Ran 9 tests in 0.001s: OK\n  $ PRODUCTION_DB=1 python3 -m unittest discover -v -s tests\n  # Ran 9 tests in 0.001s: OK\n  ```\n","duration_seconds":355.88488,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":292471,"output_tokens":81526,"thinking_tokens":67830,"cache_read_tokens":2990934,"total_tokens":373997}}}
